                           <th>Conclusion and Recommendations based on this report and previous findings known to us:</th>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                           <td>The patient’s HbA1c is significantly elevated, indicating poor long-term glycemic control and likely diabetes mellitus. This increases the risk for microvascular and macrovascular complications, especially at this advanced age. Clinical correlation and consideration of diabetes management or adjustment of current therapy are recommended.</td>
